Follow-up to #15727: Kryo 4 doesn't support records, so RemoveDanglingDeleteFilesAction.DeleteKey was rewritten as a class.
@manuzhang
@szehon-ho

PageIterator.initDataReader carries a commented-out block just after the values reader is initialized:
//    if (dataEncoding.usesDictionary() && converter.hasDictionarySupport()) {
//      bindToDictionary(dictionary);
//    } else {
//      bind(path.getType());
//    }
The referenced bindToDictionary(...) and bind(...) methods don't exist on PageIterator or its BasePageIterator superclass, so this is leftover dead code with no live counterpart — dictionary handling is already done just above via getDictionaryBasedValuesReader / getValuesReader. This removes it.
No behavior change. The meaningful TODO a few lines above is left untouched.

Backport tests from #18130 and #18061 to Spark 3.5, 4.0, 4.1.
@manuzhang
@szehon-ho

Follow-up to #18061. Tests in RemoveDanglingDeleteFilesAction run once per formatVersion, even with setupPartitionedTable(2). I replaced it with assumeThat(formatVersion).isEqualTo(2) to skip execution when formatVersion is not 2.
@manuzhang
@szehon-ho

